.²1 Inferring as the instrument of an {#anumiti#}, conclusion; from given
 premises; an inference, conclusion, one of the four means of obtaining
 knowledge according to the Nyāya system; ({#anumitikaraRamanumAnaM tacca#}
 {#DUmo vahnivyApya iti vyAptijYAnam#}. It is of two kinds {#svArTAnumAnam#}
 & {#parArTAnumAnam#}); {#pratyakzaM cAnumAnaM ca SAstraM ca viviDAgamam .#}
 {#trayaM suviditaM kAryaM DarmaSudDimaBIpsatA ..#} <ls>Ms. 12. 105</ls>.
.²2 A guess, conjecture, sign to know; {#iNgitEranumAnESca mayA jYeyA Bavizyati#} <ls>Rām.</ls>
.²3 Analogy, similarity; {#Atmano hfdayAnumAnena prekzase#} <ls>Ś. 5</ls> you judge
 (of others) by the analogy of your own heart; {#svAnumAnAtkAdambarImutprekzya#} <ls>K. 305</ls>.
.²4 (In <ab>Rhet.</ab>) A figure which consists in a notion, expressed in a peculiarly
 striking manner, of a thing established by proof; <ls>S. D. 711</ls>; {#yatra patatyabalAnAM#}
 {#dfzwirniSiMtAH patanti tatra SarAH . taccAparopitaSaro DAvatyAsAM puraH#}
 {#smaro manye .. anumAnaM taduktaM yatsADyasADanayorvacaH#} <ls>K. P. 10</ls>.
